          answer:
            "<p>One key feature of the support trench system was its location, which was positioned roughly <strong>80 metres behind the frontline trench</strong>. This second line of trenches was designed to hold <strong>reinforcement troops, ammunition, and supplies</strong> so they would be immediately available to wait and launch a counter-attack if the front line was overrun.</p><blockquote><strong>🎓 Teacher's Grading Note:</strong> <em>To secure the full 2 marks, students must identify a clear, specific feature (1 mark) and then provide a supporting sentence of contextual detail about that feature (1 mark).</em></blockquote>",
