          stimulus: [],
          answer:
            "<p>One major feature was the <strong>impassable, shell-damaged terrain</strong>, which was turned into deep quagmires of waterlogged mud by constant artillery bombardment and heavy rain. This made it impossible to use motorized transport near the front, meaning stretcher-bearers had to manually carry the wounded on foot, while horse-drawn ambulances had to be pulled by <strong>six horses instead of the usual two</strong> and severely shook patients, frequently worsening their injuries.</p><blockquote><strong>🎓 Teacher's Grading Note:</strong> <em>Students often lose marks here by writing about the soil causing infection. While historically true, this does not answer the specific question about the problems of <strong>transporting</strong> the wounded. Keeping the feature and supporting detail strictly focused on transport logistics is the key to full marks.</em></blockquote>",
